34,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000075415","module":"turquoise","kme":0.146636,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.415372,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000075415","entrez_id":["5250"],"uniprot":["Q00325"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene catalyzes the transport of phosphate into the mitochondrial matrix, either by proton cotransport or in exchange for hydroxyl ions. The protein contains three related segments arranged in tandem which are related to those found in other characterized members of the mitochondrial carrier family. Both the N-terminal and C-terminal regions of this protein protrude toward the cytosol. Multiple alternatively spliced transcript variants have been isolated. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q00325","text":"Inorganic ion transporter that transports phosphate or copper ions across the mitochondrial inner membrane into the matrix compartment (By similarity) (PubMed:17273968, PubMed:29237729). Mediates proton-coupled symport of phosphate ions necessary for mitochondrial oxidative phosphorylation of ADP to ATP (By similarity) (PubMed:17273968). Transports copper ions probably in the form of anionic copper(I) complexes to maintain mitochondrial matrix copper pool and to supply copper for cytochrome C oxidase complex assembly (PubMed:29237729). May also play a role in regulation of the mitochondrial permeability transition pore (mPTP) (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}